- **Mahler shape-deficit (E2.20):** 22% q=2-attributable; sequentially closes 84% by Q=29. NOT parity-sourced as the project implicitly assumed.
- **BDJ m_4 (E2.31):** 83% q=2-attributable; closes 95% by Q=29. Parity-dominant (matches S204).
- **Newman L^∞ (E2.21):** 100% q=2 by construction.

**Hierarchy of major-arc concentration** across the three "parity-fingerprint" edges is **NOT uniform** — the q=2 attribution fraction inverts from 100% (L^∞) to 83% (m_4) to 22% (Mahler). The mechanism distinction is log-flat-integral (Mahler) vs L^4-power-sum (m_4).

